# The build context is what `COPY` can reach. Everything here is either
# installed inside the image instead, or belongs to how the set is authored and
# checked rather than to what a client connects to.

# Installed by `npm ci` in the image. Copying the host's tree in would carry a
# Windows-native or otherwise mismatched install into a Linux image.
node_modules

# Version control, and the editor state that goes with it.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# This is why the image cannot run its own suite: `.dockerignore` excludes
# test/ from the context, so `npm test` has nothing to run inside the
# container. The suite is a gate on the repository, not on the artifact.
test
coverage

# Documentation and the agent instruction set. None of it is served.
wiki
.agents
AGENTS.md
README.md

# Local MCP server clones. Directory-shaped, so a stray clone in a working
# checkout would bloat the context without being ignored.
mcps

# The build files themselves, and a compose file if one is ever added. Harmless
# to list a file that does not exist yet.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml

# Local machine state and secrets. `.env` is gitignored and must stay out of
# the context for the same reason.
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# .gitattributes is deliberately NOT here. It is one line,
# `* text=auto eol=lf`, and it is load-bearing for this build: a CRLF after any
# instruction in this Dockerfile fails the build at line 2 with
# `\r is not a valid separator`, and a CRLF-terminated .dockerignore does not
# match the patterns it names. See wiki/environments/docker.md.
